# If nothing said who the two closures are that meet at a place, a call of what lies there could be nothing but a call of an unknown function. The call is a caller of each of the two: what it passes arrives at the parameters of both, so every caller of both is known. Neither may take what a walk has left at a call for all that arrives: the call has two callees.
# If the set were a proof, every place that it reaches would have to check it, and a wrong set would stop a right program: it is what held() expects, and linked() proves a function.
# function take(f) { return f(1); }  take(first);  take(second);
# RUN(HELD): link held functions mechanisms=all
# HELD: function f1
# HELD-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=f2|f3
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK: function f1 callers-known
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=function
# CHECK: function f2 callers-known
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=int[0, 2147483647]
# CHECK: function f3 callers-known
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 {{*}}proven=int[0, 2147483647]
# RUN(NEVER): link functions calls mechanisms=all
# NEVER-NOT: function f2 callers-known one-callee
# NEVER-NOT: function f3 callers-known one-callee
# NEVER-NOT: call f1
# Outside of a loop nothing tests for several closures at once: the tests and the arms would cost more than the call by value.
# RUN(WALK): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# WALK-NOT: testedType=f2

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = NewClosure function=f1
    v1 = NewClosure function=f2
    v2 = NewClosure function=f3
    v3 = Call v0, -, v1 calleeName="take"
    v4 = Call v0, -, v2 calleeName="take"
    v5 = Undefined
    Return v5
}
function f1 name="take" module=m0 length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = Integer integer=1
    v2 = Call v0, -, v1 calleeName="f"
    Return v2
}
function f2 name="first" module=m0 length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    Return v0
}
function f3 name="second" module=m0 length=1 thisType={type=anything} parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
